hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2930","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bukayr, who informed us Ibn Jurayj, who informed me Musa ibn 'Uqbah, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA) that he informed him:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had his head shaved during the Farewell Pilgrimage.\""\n\nThey claimed that the one who shaved the Prophet (ﷺ) was Ma'mar ibn 'Abdullah ibn Nadlah ibn 'Awf ibn 'Ubayd ibn 'Uwayj ibn 'Adi ibn Ka'b.\n\nAbu Bakr (ibn Abi Shaybah) said: \""The Prophet (ﷺ) had his head shaved by someone from the same kind (of people) as we say: the Arabs attribute the action to the one who commands it just as they attribute it to the doer. For it is known that the Prophet (ﷺ) did not take it upon himself to shave his own head with his own hand"","" but rather he commanded another to do so. Thus"","" the action is attributed to him since he was the one who commanded it.\""\n\nCHAPTER:"""""
